# Encode and decode are on Ints.
== SOURCE
2 e_ncode 1.5
== ERROR
error[type-mismatch]: expected Int, found Float
 --> -e:1:1
  |
1 | 2 e_ncode 1.5
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  | - a whole-number literal, here an Int
  |           --- a Float literal
  = note: `e_ncode` has type Int -> Int -> Int
  = help: Int and Float do not mix: `f_loat n` makes a Float of an Int, `f_loor x` or `c_eiling x` an Int of a Float
